      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Raju lived near a village in the Sundarbans. One evening, the smell of biryani drifted from a wedding feast, and he crept closer. The aroma was so rich, so layered with spices, that he forgot all about hunting. He decided right then: he had to learn to make this.\n\nHe watched the cooks from the shadows for weeks, memorising every step. He practised in a clearing, using paws instead of hands, balancing pots on flat stones over a fire. The first few tries were disasters — burnt rice, raw meat, spices everywhere. But Raju kept at it, adjusting the flame, the timing, the balance of saffron and ghee.\n\nOne monsoon night, he finally got it right. The rice was fluffy, the meat tender, the flavours perfect. He invited the forest animals to taste it, and even the sceptical monkeys came back for seconds. Raju became known as the biryani tiger, the only predator in the jungle who could turn a feast into an art.\n\n5:51 AM",
